jobs.description:
ICT Security Engineer Content Delivery and Edge Services - Swatch Group

• ICT Security Engineer Content Delivery and Edge Services
• Introduction de la société
• We don't exclusively manufacture legendary watches; We keep in time with technology!
• The Swatch Group Services Ltd. has an IT Competence Center for our 16 brands, that would make Tony Stark jealous.
• Are you ready to be our Tech Talent? Then keep reading!
• Live your passion in a position where you drive innovation, work with latest technologies, and pave the way into the new digital era.
• You will meet over 250 like-minded IT Experts and together you will design innovative solutions, work on global projects and build our IT environment of tomorrow.
• For our dynamic and international team into the Systems & Infrastructure division, we are looking for a motivated:
• Description du poste
As a Security Engineer Content Delivery and Edge Services, you will design, implement, and maintain Akamai security and performance solutions to ensure the optimal security and availability of Swatch Group’s digital platforms. You will collaborate with internal teams and external providers to integrate CDN services into our infrastructure, automate workflows, and enhance global content distribution for Swatch Group brands.
• In this role, you are responsible to:
• Design, deploy, and optimize Akamai CDN solutions (Ion, Image Manager, Kona Site Defender, EdgeWorkers) for high availability and low latency;
• Implement edge caching strategies, traffic offload, and acceleration techniques to improve web performance;
• Implement and maintain security and bot management rules;
• Develop and maintain CI/CD pipelines for CDN configuration and automation;
• Collaborate with application teams to ensure seamless integration of CDN services with enterprise platforms;
• Manage infrastructure as code (IaC) for CDN and cloud environments using tools like Terraform or Ansible;
• Monitor and analyze CDN performance metrics, availability, and security posture using Akamai Control Center and analytics tools;
• Troubleshoot and resolve issues related to CDN security;
• Ensure compliance with security best practices for CDN and edge deployments;
• Profil
• Bachelor degree or equivalent in Computer Science;
• Certifications such as GIAC GWAS, Azure Security Engineer, Palo Alto PCNSE and Akamai Certified Professional are considered a plus;
• Good knowledge of enterprise security technologies: firewalls (Palo Alto, Fortinet), VPN, endpoint protection, WAF;
• Good knowledge of web application security and CDN integration across digital platforms;
• Experience with CI/CD tools (Azure DevOps, GitLab CI, CircleCI);
• Proficiency in IaC tools (Terraform, Ansible) and scripting languages (Python, Bash);
• Knowledge of web technologies (HTML, CSS, JavaScript, PHP);
• Experience with monitoring and logging tools (Prometheus, Grafana, Elastic stack);
• Compétences requises
• Professional experience of minimum 2 years in an equivalent role is expected;
• Fluent in English, French and German are a plus;
• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills;
• Effective communication across technical and non-technical teams;
• Team-oriented with a collaborative mindset;
• Resilient and adaptable under pressure;
• Detail-oriented and precise in execution;
• Proactive and self-motivated;
• Service-oriented with a strong customer focus.
• Langues
• Now, in order to blend in, socially and professionally, we certainly recommend the following languages:
• Fluent in English, French, and German are a plus
• Any other languages are welcome - we have 29 so far in the company, if you wish to add the 30th, you pretty much know what to do.
• Personne de contact
• What we offer:
• A dynamic and evolving work environment, complemented by attractive benefits:
• Continuous training to support your professional development
• Career growth opportunities through our internal mobility policy
• 5 to 6 weeks of vacation per year, depending on your age and/or position
• A 40-hour work week, in line with the collective labor agreement (CCT)
• Competitive salary and excellent social benefits
• Parental leave: up to 3 weeks for the other parent and 19 weeks for mothers
• On-site company restaurant with employer financial contribution
• Exclusive discounts on Swatch Group products and with our partners
• Sports activities and internal events to foster team spirit
• Contribution to health insurance costs
• Ready to debug your career and deploy your next challenge? 🚀 Apply now 🚀
• Just a quick note from our sysadmin: to keep things clean and green , we only accept applications through our website.
• Lieu de travail
• Longue-Rue / Länggasse 85
• 2504 Biel/Bienne (Bern)
• Suisse
• Adresse de l'entreprise
• The Swatch Group Services SA
• Chemin du Long-Champ 119
• CH-2504 Bienne
• Postuler pour ce poste
• Partagez cette annonce

